# cases.manifest -- the single source of truth for the corpus (parsed by tests/support/harness.sh).
# Columns: name  tier(smoke|full|manual)  timeout-seconds  mode(exit|oracle:<name>|diff)
#          [env=K=V;K=V] [needs=<path>] [args=a;b;c] [xfail=<code>:<grep pattern>]
#          [group=<group>[,<group>...]]
#
# tier: smoke = the everyday fast layer (run.sh smoke); full = the gate's full defense line;
#        manual = manual batches only (tight timeout or machine-side prefix; an absent needs records SKIP).
# group: the grouping filter key (--group of corpus.run / corpus.deps-pair; stacks with --tier
#        by intersection). heavy = the heaviest subset by measured wall clock (~16 entries on the gate's slowest list);
#        entries without group= belong to the implicit light group. Routine cadence: fast -> smoke ->
#        --group heavy on demand; the full set only at the end of a campaign (run.sh gate).
# mode: exit = green on exit code (the driver was already three-way compared when created, so the gate
#       pays no native cold build); oracle:<name> = stdout must equal tests/fixtures/oracles/<name>.txt byte-for-byte;
#       diff = three-way comparison against native cargo run (for real projects under corpus/projects/<name>/):
#       the cold mirvm run only asserts exit 0 (its stderr replays dependency-build warnings, not program
#       behavior); the warm rerun must match native in all three and its stdout must equal the cold stdout.
#       A space inside an env value is written %20 (e.g. RUSTFLAGS=--cap-lints%20allow -- both sides
#       silence upstream warnings, so the stderr comparison carries only the program's own output);
#       {ROOT} in args = the repo root absolute path (expanded by the shared harness's parse_args).
# Discipline: a new corpus driver must be registered here first (scripts and the gate both read this,
#       there is no second list); a driver file with no registration = a loud gate FAIL.
#
